WEBVTT

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.100
Marvelous Entertainment.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.590
If you mix these two liquids, it will freeze in an instant!

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:00.840
Big one!

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.520
Did you see the shooting star yesterday?

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:35.410
Yes, I saw it. It was amazing, wasn't it?

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:36.560
Really?

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:39.440
It's been flying a lot recently.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:43.850
I saw a lot of it.

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:44.850
I didn't know at all.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:48.850
But shooting stars are said to be a sign that something bad is going to happen.

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:49.850
Is that so?

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:51.850
That's not true.

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:53.090
Yukishiro.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:59.690
Shooting stars are small stardust floating in space.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:06.900
and be pulled by the gravity of the wind, and evaporate at an altitude of about 100 km above sea level.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:16.140
People in the past saw such a strange sight, and I think they entrusted their wishes to the shooting star.

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:24.930
But it may be better to think of it as something good than something bad.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:28.440
Well then, let's go ahead!

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.000
Or rather,

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:39.050
When Nagisa was a year old, she was in another class, so you might not know, but Yukishiro-san was called "Uchiku-jo-o", right?

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:40.680
"Uchiku-jo-o"?

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.220
And, and, and!

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:47.440
She was popular in the men's club, and she was confessed to Nakajima-kun in the Kendo club!

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:50.950
Really? Nakajima-kun was the type, after all!

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.660
That's amazing...

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:54.860
I wonder if I should eat it with my nails dyed red...

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.630
You're going to drink it, right?

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:59.190
Ah, ah, ah! I'm just going to drink it!

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.580
Nagisa is popular, too.

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:11.670
No...

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:12.760
But, but, but...

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:14.830
It's all from girls.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.740
Nagisa is popular, as expected.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:19.260
Shut up!

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:21.560
Misumi!

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:24.440
Nagisa Misumi!

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:28.020
Nagisa...

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.000
Solve this problem.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.990
Hurry up!

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:36.670
What's wrong, Misumi?

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.150
You're already in the second grade.

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.700
This is too soon, isn't it?

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:43.850
Even if you say something like that, suddenly...

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:46.150
I can't solve this problem.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:47.630
What is it, Yukishiro?

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:50.040
You can't solve it with Misumi's head?

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:50.990
Kajin!

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:52.500
But I can say it.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:54.210
No, it's not that.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:58.830
It's a strange answer called 0 = 26.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.000
What?

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:08.710
19 + x is a mistake of 19 - x, isn't it?

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:13.000
Then we can get the answer of x = 13, right?

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.580
No, it's true.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.320
Igo, be careful.

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:30.000
No, thank you.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:45.650
What?

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:52.380
I'm going to decide the next class, but how about Nagisa and Yukishiro-san?

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:57.010
Yukishiro-san who's popular with boys and Nagisa who's popular with girls, right?

00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:00.000
No, I'm not that kind of character.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:02.130
I think it's good.

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:29.920
I'm not interested in that kind of girl.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:52.810
No matter how popular he is, I want to be popular with boys sometimes.

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:56.930
What?

00:07:56.930 --> 00:08:00.000
I have to be popular so that I can make a great boyfriend.

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:04.260
I'm so hungry that I'm going to eat a lot of cake.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:04.780
Chuu-taro!

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:07.050
Did you get home?

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:09.050
I'm home, grandma!

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:11.010
Did something happen to Chuu-taro?

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:13.260
Yeah, he's probably fine.

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:20.770
Is there something here?

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.100
What?

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:12.270
You're a member?

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:21.830
Well, I can't imagine.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:22.980
Come and take a look.

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:25.490
Eh? I don't need to.

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:26.990
It's fine, just come and take a look.

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:34.630
Onee-chan, what's wrong with Mom?

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:38.990
What is it?

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:43.960
Ryota, what I'm about to show you isn't a dream. It's reality. Try to calm down.

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:47.080
It's better to calm down, Onee-chan.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.850
Actually, there's something weird here.

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:54.210
Onee-chan, you're cheating! I bought a cell phone!

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:57.760
A cell phone? No, there's a weird creature in here.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:58.780
In here?

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:00.000
H-Hey, stop it!

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:04.890
I can't hear a thing. What is this?

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:07.390
This is strange...

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:10.440
I did talk to this guy earlier, though...

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:12.370
You're not sleepy, are you?

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:13.960
It's still evening.

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:14.980
You're so annoying!

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:18.400
Ryouta, be careful!

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:20.020
M-Mom!

00:11:20.020 --> 00:11:22.010
Ms. Nagisa is talking to me again!

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:26.810
Don't tell her!

00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:27.940
Was there something like that?

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:33.100
What's this card?

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:40.980
Ah, she's walking.

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:43.480
What's wrong?

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:48.910
It's hard to move on your own after all, Meppo.

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:50.410
Hey, you girl!

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:53.760
I'm taking you to the hope princess, Whipple, Meppo!

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:55.540
Huh? What's that?

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:56.380
I don't want to!

00:11:57.220 --> 00:11:58.380
Please, Meppo!

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:00.000
There's no one else I can rely on, Meppo!

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:17.340
I said that...

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:25.570
Don't say that!

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:28.040
The right is a bent eye!

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:32.560
Come on, Po-Mepo, shut up.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.070
You can't go straight.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:36.810
I don't care. I'll go straight no matter how far I go, Po-Mepo.

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:38.830
You can't do that, can you?

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:41.650
No.

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:44.210
You're going to cry again, aren't you?

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:52.210
Who the hell are you?

00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:56.260
I'm the chosen hero from the Hikari no Sono, Meppuru-Mepo.

00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:58.530
Hikari no Sono? A hero?

00:12:58.530 --> 00:12:59.600
You?

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:19.360
I'm hungry~

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:21.440
Listen to other people's stories!

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:27.920
But?

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:30.000
In which direction?

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:33.110
I'm sure of it!

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:34.310
That's strange, Meppo.

00:13:34.310 --> 00:13:37.110
I feel something different from Nipple, Meppo.

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:38.670
What do you mean, something?

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:46.160
This is a dead end, young lady.

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:48.940
I've been looking for you.

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:50.340
Where are you?

00:13:50.340 --> 00:13:52.860
My name is Piecer.

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:55.110
I'm here to get you.

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:56.570
Run, Meppo!

00:13:56.570 --> 00:13:58.460
I think this is better!

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:09.980
Don't burn my hands.

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:14.050
Where's the stone?

00:14:14.050 --> 00:14:23.040
What do you mean?

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:25.790
That girl brought me all the way here.

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:26.670
You too?

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:27.520
Nettaro!

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.790
This is the one.

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:35.860
The other one is gone, but I don't have time to look for it.

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:38.160
I'll give it to you, too.

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:03.840
What are you talking about?

00:17:08.830 --> 00:17:09.800
What happened?

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:43.830
Honey?

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:48.430
You're so annoying, kids.

00:18:48.430 --> 00:18:51.440
You're a madman, you're a madman!

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:55.120
You evil spirit, let me see the terror of darkness!

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:42.570
Really?

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:44.020
Alright, don't mess with me!

00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:48.280
Sekurume-po!

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:09.360
This is dangerous, Meppo!

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:18.340
Dog, connect with me, Meppo!

00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:33.680
What's going on?

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:41.480
Who the hell are they?

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:45.520
Mashiro...

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:05.860
I'm sorry for interrupting, but I want you to explain something.

00:22:05.860 --> 00:22:08.960
You have the power of Precure, Meppo!

00:22:08.960 --> 00:22:11.410
Precure?

00:22:11.410 --> 00:22:14.410
Come to think of it, I think I said that myself...

00:22:14.410 --> 00:22:19.200
From now on, the two of you will fight with us as Precure, the messenger of light!

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:23.620
I don't want you to decide it yourself!

00:22:23.620 --> 00:22:25.620
We'll take care of you, Meppo!

00:22:25.620 --> 00:22:27.360
We'll be in your care from now on!

00:22:30.640 --> 00:22:33.040
It looks interesting!

00:24:14.200 --> 00:24:15.580
But we have no choice but to do it.

00:24:15.580 --> 00:24:17.030
Hey, don't you think it's too much?

00:24:17.030 --> 00:24:18.180
Oh, my God!

00:24:33.610 --> 00:24:37.840
Honestly, honestly, honestly, honestly!

00:24:37.840 --> 00:24:44.110
Ishizawa-san, Yukishiro-san.

00:24:44.110 --> 00:24:49.640
Suddenly, a strange guy came from the other side of the sky.

00:24:49.640 --> 00:24:55.380
When he was following Yuga-mama, Yukishiro-san appeared like the same guy.

00:24:55.380 --> 00:25:00.000
Then, he was attacked by a roller coaster ghost, and when he noticed...

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:03.000
We transformed and fought against the ghosts.

00:25:03.000 --> 00:25:05.510
Who came to our house?

00:25:05.510 --> 00:25:11.540
Who attacked us?

00:25:14.050 --> 00:25:16.050
I can't believe I transformed.

00:25:16.050 --> 00:25:19.600
I wonder if I was dreaming.

00:25:20.630 --> 00:25:22.800
As a result of the voting,

00:25:22.800 --> 00:25:26.720
Yukishiro will be the class president of the 2-year Sakura class.

00:25:26.720 --> 00:25:28.800
Thank you for your cooperation.

00:25:34.380 --> 00:25:38.780
Tami-san is like Nogiku. I love Nogiku.

00:25:38.780 --> 00:25:39.870
Oi oi!

00:25:39.870 --> 00:25:42.490
Then Tami-san said "Oi oi".

00:25:43.490 --> 00:25:44.400
What?

00:25:46.570 --> 00:25:47.450
It's her!

00:25:47.450 --> 00:25:49.930
What's wrong, Misumi-san?

00:25:49.930 --> 00:25:51.710
Nothing.

00:25:52.490 --> 00:25:53.890
Continue.

00:25:53.890 --> 00:25:54.680
Yes!

00:25:54.680 --> 00:25:58.010
Then Tami-san said "Oi oi oi"!

00:25:58.010 --> 00:25:59.160
Misumi-san...

00:27:24.510 --> 00:27:30.000
Lord Jerk King, I have found two of them that escaped from the Garden of Light.

00:27:31.400 --> 00:27:37.840
I see. Then why is there no Prism Stone here right now?

00:27:37.840 --> 00:27:38.800
That's because...

00:27:38.800 --> 00:27:40.500
There's an unexpected obstacle.

00:27:40.500 --> 00:27:43.890
I don't want to hear about that!

00:27:43.890 --> 00:27:45.640
Prism Stone...

00:27:45.640 --> 00:27:49.040
Of the seven, five are already in my hands.

00:27:49.040 --> 00:27:52.050
Kirise, your mission is...

00:27:52.050 --> 00:27:56.560
To take the remaining two that they took with them.

00:27:56.560 --> 00:27:58.390
I understand.

00:27:58.390 --> 00:28:00.000
If I can survive...

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:04.030
I need the power to create everything that Trism Stone possesses.

00:28:04.030 --> 00:28:09.120
When all seven stones are gathered, I will become an eternal being.

00:28:09.120 --> 00:28:17.830
And my DOSKZONE will conquer all the worlds and rule them one by one!

00:28:17.830 --> 00:28:22.000
Go, P-3rd! For the sake of our future!

00:28:30.830 --> 00:28:42.200
A town targeted by the sea!

00:28:42.200 --> 00:28:43.820
What on earth are you doing in the middle of the night?

00:28:43.820 --> 00:28:47.360
I'm hungry, Meppo. Nagisa, give me breakfast.

00:28:47.360 --> 00:28:51.680
You're kidding, right? I'm not your wife!

00:28:51.680 --> 00:28:54.820
Besides, don't call me like that.

00:28:54.820 --> 00:28:57.350
Then please, Nagisa-sama.

00:28:57.350 --> 00:29:00.000
Nagisa-oneesuman.

00:29:00.160 --> 00:29:03.550
Hatsuhime!

00:29:03.550 --> 00:29:07.020
Eh, eh, eh!

00:29:07.020 --> 00:29:09.400
Meppo, if that's the case...

00:29:09.400 --> 00:29:10.240
Hm?

00:29:10.240 --> 00:29:11.700
Are you going to quit, Meppo?

00:29:11.700 --> 00:29:13.200
If I quit...

00:29:13.200 --> 00:29:15.840
I'm quitting, so give me some food, Meppo!

00:29:15.840 --> 00:29:19.240
But I don't have anything to eat.

00:29:19.240 --> 00:29:22.020
I'll be throwing away the card I'm taking care of, Meppo!

00:29:22.020 --> 00:29:23.080
Card?

00:29:23.080 --> 00:29:26.550
If you don't throw away the card, you won't be able to eat any food, Meppo!

00:29:26.550 --> 00:29:27.910
Geez...

00:29:30.090 --> 00:29:31.480
What card is that?

00:29:31.480 --> 00:29:32.780
Omppu-meppo.

00:29:32.780 --> 00:29:35.180
Omppu? What is that?

00:29:35.180 --> 00:29:38.880
That card is for the 10 people in the Shrine of Light.

00:29:38.880 --> 00:29:41.770
They came to take care of me-meppo.

00:29:41.770 --> 00:29:43.190
This one?

00:29:43.190 --> 00:29:45.810
No-meppo.

00:29:45.810 --> 00:29:47.020
Then this one.

00:29:47.020 --> 00:29:49.520
No-meppo.

00:29:49.520 --> 00:29:50.020
This one?

00:29:50.020 --> 00:29:51.590
No-meppo.

00:29:51.590 --> 00:29:53.440
Then what about this one?

00:29:53.440 --> 00:29:55.820
That's Omppu-meppo.

00:29:55.820 --> 00:29:56.720
This one?

00:29:56.720 --> 00:30:00.000
Hurry up and slash it-meppo.

00:30:02.040 --> 00:30:05.320
Good morning, Mr. Meppuru.

00:30:08.450 --> 00:30:11.990
This morning, I prepared a bacon-lettuce sandwich.

00:30:11.990 --> 00:30:15.670
It looks delicious!

00:30:15.670 --> 00:30:19.130
It's the last one, isn't it?

00:30:19.950 --> 00:30:21.510
You're so selfish.

00:30:21.510 --> 00:30:22.950
How many times have I told you, Meppo?

00:30:22.950 --> 00:30:25.980
N-No, but wouldn't it be nice if we did it here?

00:30:25.980 --> 00:30:27.360
Hmm?

00:30:27.360 --> 00:30:29.480
For breakfast, we'll have some rice and miso soup.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:32.000
I'm glad I was born a man.

00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:34.000
Who are you talking about?

00:30:34.000 --> 00:30:49.300
Even so, what is this energy?

00:30:49.300 --> 00:30:52.780
The quality of each one falls,

00:30:52.780 --> 00:30:56.660
but I feel the power to create small things everywhere.

00:30:56.660 --> 00:30:57.660
That's not all.

00:30:57.660 --> 00:31:00.000
Countless joys and sorrows,

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:04.850
Even anger and hatred become overflowing with power.

00:31:04.850 --> 00:31:05.960
As if...

00:31:05.960 --> 00:31:06.820
That's right.

00:31:06.820 --> 00:31:09.090
It's like a huge power furnace.

00:31:09.090 --> 00:31:13.780
I think the Dark King will be able to get a good souvenir.

00:31:13.780 --> 00:31:19.620
Yukishiro-san's?

00:31:19.620 --> 00:31:21.580
Yes, it's a self-made one.

00:31:22.580 --> 00:31:23.580
Please take a look.

00:31:23.580 --> 00:31:26.820
If you add this sugar water...

00:31:32.680 --> 00:31:33.740
Are you okay?

00:31:33.740 --> 00:31:34.200
Yeah.

00:31:34.200 --> 00:31:48.080
That's all?

00:32:01.600 --> 00:32:02.690
Yukishiro-san...

00:32:03.420 --> 00:32:05.910
Mipple is nearby, Mepo!

00:32:05.910 --> 00:32:12.630
Mipple, Mipple, Mipple, Mipple, Mipple, where are you, Mepo?

00:32:12.630 --> 00:32:15.010
I'm taking a nap right now.

00:32:15.010 --> 00:32:19.550
You've become like this, Mepo!

00:32:19.550 --> 00:32:23.840
You're tired of wasting your energy, Mepo.

00:32:23.840 --> 00:32:27.460
You really wanted to meet Mipple, didn't you?

00:32:27.460 --> 00:32:30.000
You mean the love that was tied tightly?

00:32:30.190 --> 00:32:34.150
But even during class, I can't help but talk about anything, so I'm in trouble.

00:32:34.150 --> 00:32:36.950
Oh, a sleeping card?

00:32:36.950 --> 00:32:38.230
A sleeping card?

00:32:38.230 --> 00:32:39.030
Yeah.

00:32:39.030 --> 00:32:40.950
Did you have one like this?

00:32:40.950 --> 00:32:41.930
Which one?

00:32:41.930 --> 00:32:42.990
This one.

00:32:42.990 --> 00:32:44.270
Oh, no!

00:32:44.270 --> 00:32:46.230
I'm not sleepy right now, Mepo!

00:32:46.230 --> 00:32:47.230
Be quiet!

00:32:52.250 --> 00:33:00.000
It's true.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:01.380
I fell asleep.

00:33:01.380 --> 00:33:04.040
Let's let her sleep at school.

00:33:04.040 --> 00:33:05.900
That's right.

00:33:05.900 --> 00:33:06.870
So?

00:33:06.870 --> 00:33:08.980
You have something to tell me, right?

00:33:08.980 --> 00:33:09.810
Yeah.

00:33:09.810 --> 00:33:12.410
I don't want to do that anymore.

00:33:12.410 --> 00:33:13.740
